>> title: Chocolate Pots de Crème
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: chocolate, custard, cream, oven, make-ahead
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: pot de crème, pots de creme, chocolate custard pot
>> servings: 6
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — thirty-five minutes and a centre that still wobbles; past that the egg sets hard and grainy, and rebaking only makes it worse

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (165°C) and set six #6-oz ramekins{} in a roasting pan.

Heat @heavy cream{1 1/2%cup}(360 mL), @whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @table salt{1/4%tsp} in a #saucepan{} until steaming.

>> step: melt in, whisk smooth
Melt @bittersweet chocolate{6%oz}(170 g, chopped), @espresso powder{1/2%tsp}(1 g) in @&(~1)hot cream{}, whisking smooth.

Whisk @egg yolks{6%large}(110 g), @granulated sugar{1/3%cup}(65 g), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) to a pale ribbon.

Temper @&(~1)yolks{} with @&(~2)chocolate cream{}.

>> step: bake at 325°F in a water bath 35 min
Strain @&(~1)custard{} into the ramekins, pour hot water halfway up their sides, and bake at 325°F for ~{35%min}.

Chill @&(~1)pots de creme{} for ~{3%hr}.
